another very public reappearance of the  tennis star who vanished after she  accused a senior communist party  official of sexual assault  this time at an event to promote the  beijing winter olympics and miss pong  addressed those allegations for the  first time speaking to a reporter from  singaporean newspaper liane herzel who  happened to bump into her  firstly i want to emphasize that it's  very important i never said nor wrote  that i was sexually assaulted  i must emphasize that point clearly  then about weibo it's my privacy  maybe people have some misunderstanding  this was the post that pong made on  weibo a social media site in november in  it she does not use the chinese term for  sexual assault but she does say that jan  gao lee a very high ranking official  forced her into sex the post was removed  from the internet in just 20 minutes and  nothing was heard from pong for weeks  but then chinese state media posted  videos of miss pang in beijing along  with an email they said she'd written to  the head of the women's tennis  association to many it looks stage  managed and it did not convince the wta  which has suspended tournaments in china  as a result in a statement on monday the  organization said it still had  significant concerns about her  well-being and ability to communicate  without censorship or coercion  we remain steadfast in our call for a  full fair and transparent investigation  without censorship into her allegation  of sexual assault  ever since she reappeared we've only  seen pung through other people's videos  her weibo account where she spoke in her  own voice with great feeling and  intensity remains censored tom cheshire  sky news beijing
 

